zen_split its\\n# exp-only decode is cheap too, so it crosses over late — see the table below.)\\n# Measure T_decomp per codec with benchmarks/weight_compress.py on an idle GPU\\n# (its d_ms decompress-latency column, summed over the qkv/o/gateup/down fused\\n# weights), feed it through the slack model above, and paste the result here.\\n# Codecs absent from this dict fall back to\\n# _PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK_GLOBAL_DEFAULT (= prior single-threshold behaviour).\\n# The env var TIERED_SERVE_PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK overrides both: a single int\\n# forces one global threshold; \\\"<codec>=<n>,...\\\" sets per-codec values.\\n_PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK_GLOBAL_DEFAULT = 1330\\n# Threshold = (T_load_raw_bf16 - T_decomp) / T_gemm_per_token, i.e. how many\\n# tokens of GEMM fit in the slack the raw-H2D path has over the decode path.\\n# This is CONFIG-AGGREGATE, not per-weight: T_load_raw and T_decomp depend on\\n# the residency layout, so the SAME codec has different thresholds in different\\n# configs. The values here are for the frozen_split configs (cao family);\\n# offload_compressed configs use _OFFLOAD_PREFILL_MAX_CHUNK_DEFAULTS.\\n#\\n# Two effects make frozen_split (e.g. cao) carry a HIGH threshold:\\n#   * frozen_split decode is EXP-ONLY (sm stays HBM) — far cheaper than the\\n#     offload full-blob decompress, so T_decomp is small.\\n#   * with all layers frozen_split, every layer loads raw (large T_load_raw).\\n#   => big slack => large threshold.\\n#   codec      thr    source\\n#   p4flat     1330   hand-calibrated 400ms cao-p4flat operating point\\n#                     (exp-only decomp 72 / load_raw 364 -> slack 292).\\n#   zipserv    1107   cao slack model: load_raw 364 / exp-only decomp 121 ->\\n#                     slack 243 -> 1330*243/292 = ~1107. zipserv's triple-\\n#                     bitmap exp decode is HEAVIER than p4flat's palette\\n#                     (121 vs 72ms), so it crosses over to raw_bf16 earlier.\\n#   ublb_flat  1367   } synthetic isolated bench (palette/data-independent);\\n#   p4d16      1206   } refine with the slack model if used under a real config.\\n#   dietgpu     670   STALE synthetic. ANS+data-dependent — re-derive.\\n_PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK_DEFAULTS = {\\n    \\\"p4flat\\\": 1330,\\n    \\\"ublb_flat\\\": 1367,\\n    \\\"p4d16\\\": 1206,\\n    \\\"zipserv\\\": 1107,   # cao (frozen_split): slack 243 (decomp 121) -> ~1107\\n    \\\"dietgpu\\\": 670,    # TODO: re-derive with the slack model on a real config\\n}\\n\\n# Codecs whose decompress is BIT-EXACT w.r.t. the original BF16 weight, so\\n# decoding them during prefill is lossless. FP8 cells (zipserv_fp8, dietgpu_fp8,\\n# p3flat_fp8) quantize, so offload_compressed prefill must keep their\\n# uncompressed copy (see the \\\"for accuracy\\\" branch in _get_weight_source).\\n_LOSSLESS_OFFLOAD_CODECS = frozenset({\\n    \\\"zipserv\\\", \\\"dietgpu\\\", \\\"zipserv_bf16\\\", \\\"dietgpu_bf16\\\",\\n    \\\"p4flat\\\", \\\"p4d16\\\", \\\"ublb_flat\\\",\\n    \\\"chunk_delta3\\\",\\n})\\n\\n# Phase-adaptive prefill for offload_compressed weights (see _get_weight_source).\\n# offload_compressed already keeps BOTH a compressed and an uncompressed LPDDR\\n# copy; today prefill ALWAYS H2Ds the uncompressed one (no chunk gating). Below\\n# this per-codec chunk threshold, prefill instead H2Ds + FULL-decompresses the\\n# compressed copy. Same slack model as the frozen_split knob\\n# (thr = (T_load_raw - T_decomp)/T_gemm_per_token) but with DISTINCT inputs:\\n# offload does the FULL-blob decompress (vs frozen_split's cheap exp-only), so\\n# T_decomp is much larger, AND offload configs (e.g. flexgen-comp) typically\\n# keep half the layers frozen_uncompressed, so fewer layers load -> smaller\\n# T_load_raw. Both shrink the slack -> a MUCH lower threshold than frozen_split.\\n#   codec    thr   source\\n#   zipserv  384   flexgen-comp slack model: load_raw 182 / full decomp 109 ->\\n#                  slack 73 -> 384 (vs cao's 1330 — same codec, different config).\\n# Codecs without an entry resolve to 0 (disabled = always-uncompressed prefill,\\n# i.e. unchanged behaviour). Per-config; override via\\n# TIERED_SERVE_OFFLOAD_PREFILL_MAX_CHUNK (same \\\"<codec>=<n>,...|<int>\\\" syntax).\\n_OFFLOAD_PREFILL_MAX_CHUNK_DEFAULTS = {\\n    \\\"zipserv\\\": 384,   # flexgen-comp (offload, full decompress -> small slack)\\n}\\n\\n_ENV_FROZEN_DETAILED_NVTX = (\\n    os.getenv(\\\"TIERED_SERVE_FROZEN_DETAILED_NVTX\\\", \\\"0\\\") == \\\"1\\\")\\n_ENV_WLOAD_GRAPH = os.getenv(\\\"TIERED_SERVE_WLOAD_GRAPH\\\", \\\"0\\\") == \\\"1\\\"\\n_ENV_WLOAD_GRAPH_SEPARATE = (\\n    os.getenv(\\\"TIERED_SERVE_WLOAD_GRAPH_SEPARATE\\\", \\\"0\\\") == \\\"1\\\")\\n_ENV_ANY_WLOAD_GRAPH = _ENV_WLOAD_GRAPH or _ENV_WLOAD_GRAPH_SEPARATE\\n\\n\\nclass FrozenSplitMixin:\\n\\n    def _shrink_dietgpu_decompress_workspaces(self) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Shrink every DietGPU weight compressor's ANS workspace to the\\n        decompress-only size now that all weights are compressed.\\n\\n        The workspace is auto-sized for the compress peak (~1.4x the\\n        largest weight, e.g. ~627 MiB for Llama-70B's gate_up_proj).  ANS\\n        *decompress* only carves an O(numInBatch) decode table (~KB,\\n        independent of the stream size), so holding the compress-sized\\n        buffer for the whole serving run wastes ~0.6 GiB per DietGPU\\n        instance.  Reclaiming it before KV-cache / CUDA-graph allocation\\n        is often the difference between fitting and OOM on dietgpu-heavy\\n        plans.  ``compress`` self-restores the large workspace if a\\n        runtime reconfigure compresses again.\\n\\n        Tunable / disable via ``TIERED_SERVE_DIETGPU_DECOMPRESS_WS_MIB``\\n        (default 16 MiB; <= 0 disables the shrink).\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not DualMemoryLoader.use_weight_comp:\\n            return\\n        target = int(\\n            os.getenv(\\\"TIERED_SERVE_DIETGPU_DECOMPRESS_WS_MIB\\\", \\\"16\\\")) << 20\\n       